hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"176","Dhahaba al-ẓama', wa ibtallat al-‘urūq, wa thabata al-ajru in shā’ Allāh.. The thirst has gone, the veins are moistened, and the reward is established, if God wills."
"177","Allāhumma innī as'aluka bi raḥmatika ‘l-latī wasi`at kulla shay' an taghfira lī. O Allah, I ask You by Your mercy, which encompasses all things, that You forgive me. Reference: Ibn Majah 1/557 from a supplication of Abdullah bin 'Amr. Al-Hafidh graded it as good in his checking of An-Nawawi's Kitabul-'Athkdr. See Sharhul- Athkar 4/342."
